00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:27.260
 probabilistic classifier based on applying Bayez theorem with strong, also called naive

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:34.220
 independence assumptions between the features. So let's learn about the Bayez theorem first.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.960
 It says that the probability of an event A given another event B can be calculated as the probability

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:49.220
 of B given A times the probability of A divided by the probability of B. So if we transfer this to our

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:56.460
 case with class labels and features, then we can say that the probability of Y given X is the

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:03.740
 probability of X given Y times the probability of Y divided by the probability of X. And in this

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:11.120
 case, Y are the class labels that we want to predict and X is the feature vector. So then we do the

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:17.020
 assumption that the features are mutually independent. For example, if we want to predict if

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:23.980
 someone takes the bus or walks, and we have two features if it's raining or not, and the distance to

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:30.300
 the destination. So then we make the assumption that these two features are independent. And in reality,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.660
 often this is not the case. But this assumption still works really well for this classifier. That's

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:42.220
 also why we say this is a naive assumption. So if you make this assumption, we can split this part here,

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:49.500
 p of x given y into the different components and say this is the product. So p of x1 given y times p of

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:57.260
 x2 given y and so on. And these are all the single feature vector components. And these probabilities here

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:05.100
 are easier to set up. So now we want to select the class label y. So we want to select the class with the

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:13.420
 highest posterior probability. So this p of y given x is also called the posterior. And this is the formula

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:21.100
